  "verbalization": "Trelagliptin is associated with Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus through a chain of indications that ultimately link it to the disease. The evidence suggests that Trelagliptin is indicated for Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus, and this condition is indicated for drugs like Voglibose, Albiglutide, and Gemigliptin, all of which are also indicated for Diabetes Mellitus (disease). This creates a cascading relationship where Trelagliptin is indirectly linked to the disease through these indicated drugs. The strength of the evidence is supported by multiple paths with high scores, indicating a consistent pattern across different indications. The mechanism appears to involve the use of drugs that are used to manage diabetes, suggesting a potential role in the treatment of the condition. The integration of these paths highlights the indirect relationship between Trelagliptin and Diabetes Mellitus, emphasizing the importance of drug indications in linking therapeutic agents to diseases.",
